the european commission has created a  set of online tools to help you get  going with levels the eu approach to  assess and report on the sustainability  of buildings first there's an e-learning  program hosted on the eu academy  platform it's the best place to start  when preparing to use levels in your  working environment the e-learning  program is designed for all kinds of  built environment professionals and  shows you how to apply levels at all  stages of a building's life cycle it's  fully customizable too  so whether you're involved in the  planning design financing or completion  of the building the levels e-learning  program is for you  the program also includes a case study  exploring how each levels indicator can  be used throughout the life cycle of a  building step by step you'll see how you  can cut emissions save natural resources  and improve occupants quality of life  the aim is to give you the knowledge and  motivation to complete your first  building assessment using levels  as well as the e-learning program levels  offers a free calculation and assessment  tool making it easier to measure  sustainability performance on your  project you can use the tool to create a  project and start an assessment  choose your indicators complete your  assessment and compare your assessment  results  we hope these resources will help make  your building project more sustainable  access the e-learning program and  calculator tool today through the levels  website
 

